course: dictionary
lesson: 11462
title: Words for growing up
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An adolescent is a young person who is growing from a child into an adult. Most adolescents are aged about 12 to 18, and we often call them teenagers.
explain: «My cousin is an adolescent now. She has started high school and is growing taller every month.» The clues are high school and growing taller. She is not a little child, but she is not yet an adult.
explain: Adolescent can also be an adjective, describing things to do with this time of life, as in «adolescent health». It can also be used to criticise. «Slamming the door and sulking is very adolescent» means the behaviour is silly and immature.
fact: An adolescent is a young person, usually aged about 12 to 18, who is growing from a child into an adult.
fact: «Adolescent» can be a noun («an adolescent») or an adjective («adolescent years»).
fact: «Adolescent» is a more formal word for «teenager», and you will often see it in health books and leaflets.
fact: Puberty is the time when a child's body starts to change, and it often happens during adolescence.
fact: When someone says «adolescent behaviour» in a disapproving way, they mean silly or immature, like a teenager showing off.
exercise: «Mia is twelve and is growing up fast, so she is now an adolescent.» What is an adolescent? | An old person who has retired | A baby who cannot walk yet | *A young person growing from a child into an adult | A type of fast car
exercise: «The health leaflet was written for adolescents, aged about 12 to 18.» Who is the leaflet for? | Very old people | *Teenagers | Adults who are fully grown | Young children under five
exercise: Ravi says, «That was a bit adolescent of you, slamming the door and sulking.» What does adolescent suggest here? | Old and tired | *Silly and immature | Very wise and calm | Kind and helpful
test: Which word means the same as «teenager» in a health book? | Infant | Toddler | Elder | *Adolescent
test: Which sentence uses «adolescent» to mean silly or immature? | «She is an adolescent of twelve.» | *«Stop being so adolescent about the game.» | «The adolescents met at the bus stop.» | «The adolescent years are a time of change.»
exam: Which word means a young person growing from a child into an adult, usually aged 12 to 18? | Adult | Infant | *Adolescent | Pensioner
